{
  "id": "u02",
  "section": 1,
  "order": 2,
  "title": "Family & people",
  "teTitle": "కుటుంబం",
  "cefr": "A1+",
  "register": "standard",
  "description": "Introduce your family, ask about someone's family, and talk about ages.",
  "items": [
    {
      "id": "u02-i01",
      "te": "ఈయన మా నాన్న.",
      "gloss": "This is my father.",
      "words": [
        { "te": "ఈయన", "gloss": "this man (respectful)" },
        { "te": "మా", "gloss": "our / my (family)" },
        { "te": "నాన్న", "gloss": "dad" }
      ],
      "tags": ["family", "introductions"],
      "difficulty": 1,
      "note": "Telugu says మా (maa, 'our') for your own parents — మా నాన్న, మా అమ్మ — because family is shared. Use నా (naa, 'my') for things only yours.",
      "distractors": ["u02-i02", "u02-i03"]
    },
    {
      "id": "u02-i02",
      "te": "ఈవిడ మా అమ్మ.",
      "gloss": "This is my mother.",
      "words": [
        { "te": "ఈవిడ", "gloss": "this woman (respectful)" },
        { "te": "మా", "gloss": "our / my (family)" },
        { "te": "అమ్మ", "gloss": "mom" }
      ],
      "tags": ["family", "introductions"],
      "difficulty": 1,
      "distractors": ["u02-i01", "u02-i04"]
    },
    {
      "id": "u02-i03",
      "te": "వీడు నా తమ్ముడు.",
      "gloss": "This is my younger brother.",
      "words": [
        { "te": "వీడు", "gloss": "this guy (casual)" },
        { "te": "నా", "gloss": "my" },
        { "te": "తమ్ముడు", "gloss": "younger brother" }
      ],
      "tags": ["family", "introductions"],
      "difficulty": 1,
      "note": "వీడు (viiDu) is casual — perfect for your little brother, rude for anyone else. For a stranger use ఇతను (itanu) or the respectful ఈయన (iiyana)."
    },
    {
      "id": "u02-i04",
      "te": "ఈమె నా చెల్లి.",
      "gloss": "This is my younger sister.",
      "words": [
        { "te": "ఈమె", "gloss": "this girl / woman" },
        { "te": "నా", "gloss": "my" },
        { "te": "చెల్లి", "gloss": "younger sister" }
      ],
      "tags": ["family", "introductions"],
      "difficulty": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "u02-i05",
      "te": "మీ ఇంట్లో ఎంతమంది ఉన్నారు?",
      "gloss": "How many people are in your house?",
      "words": [
        { "te": "మీ", "gloss": "your (polite)" },
        { "te": "ఇంట్లో", "gloss": "in the house" },
        { "te": "ఎంతమంది", "gloss": "how many people" },
        { "te": "ఉన్నారు", "gloss": "are (there)" }
      ],
      "tags": ["family", "questions"],
      "difficulty": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "u02-i06",
      "te": "మేము నలుగురం.",
      "gloss": "We are four (people).",
      "words": [
        { "te": "మేము", "gloss": "we" },
        { "te": "నలుగురం", "gloss": "four of us" }
      ],
      "tags": ["family", "numbers"],
      "difficulty": 2,
      "note": "People get special numbers: ఇద్దరు (iddaru) two, ముగ్గురు (mugguru) three, నలుగురు (naluguru) four. మేము నలుగురం = 'we are four'.",
      "distractors": ["u02-i12", "u02-i08"]
    },
    {
      "id": "u02-i07",
      "te": "మీకు అక్క ఉందా?",
      "gloss": "Do you have an elder sister?",
      "words": [
        { "te": "మీకు", "gloss": "to you (polite)" },
        { "te": "అక్క", "gloss": "elder sister" },
        { "te": "ఉందా", "gloss": "is there?" }
      ],
      "tags": ["family", "questions"],
      "difficulty": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "u02-i08",
      "te": "లేదు, నాకు అన్నయ్య ఉన్నాడు.",
      "gloss": "No, I have an elder brother.",
      "words": [
        { "te": "లేదు", "gloss": "no / there isn't" },
        { "te": "నాకు", "gloss": "to me" },
        { "te": "అన్నయ్య", "gloss": "elder brother" },
        { "te": "ఉన్నాడు", "gloss": "he is (there)" }
      ],
      "tags": ["family"],
      "difficulty": 2,
      "distractors": ["u02-i06", "u02-i07"]
    },
    {
      "id": "u02-i09",
      "te": "అమ్మమ్మ ఊళ్ళో ఉంటుంది.",
      "gloss": "Grandma lives in the village.",
      "words": [
        { "te": "అమ్మమ్మ", "gloss": "grandma (mother's mother)" },
        { "te": "ఊళ్ళో", "gloss": "in the village / hometown" },
        { "te": "ఉంటుంది", "gloss": "she lives / stays" }
      ],
      "tags": ["family"],
      "difficulty": 2,
      "note": "అమ్మమ్మ (ammamma) is your mother's mother; your father's mother is నానమ్మ (naanamma). Telugu never mixes them up!"
    },
    {
      "id": "u02-i10",
      "te": "తాతయ్య మాతో ఉంటారు.",
      "gloss": "Grandpa lives with us.",
      "words": [
        { "te": "తాతయ్య", "gloss": "grandpa" },
        { "te": "మాతో", "gloss": "with us" },
        { "te": "ఉంటారు", "gloss": "he lives (respectful)" }
      ],
      "tags": ["family"],
      "difficulty": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "u02-i11",
      "te": "నీకు ఎన్ని ఏళ్ళు?",
      "gloss": "How old are you? (informal)",
      "words": [
        { "te": "నీకు", "gloss": "to you (informal)" },
        { "te": "ఎన్ని", "gloss": "how many" },
        { "te": "ఏళ్ళు", "gloss": "years" }
      ],
      "tags": ["age", "questions"],
      "difficulty": 1,
      "note": "నీకు (niiku) is informal — fine for kids and close friends. To an elder, ask మీ వయసు ఎంత? (mee vayasu enta)."
    },
    {
      "id": "u02-i12",
      "te": "నాకు ఇరవై ఏళ్ళు.",
      "gloss": "I am twenty years old.",
      "words": [
        { "te": "నాకు", "gloss": "to me" },
        { "te": "ఇరవై", "gloss": "twenty" },
        { "te": "ఏళ్ళు", "gloss": "years" }
      ],
      "tags": ["age"],
      "difficulty": 1,
      "distractors": ["u02-i13", "u02-i06"]
    },
    {
      "id": "u02-i13",
      "te": "చెల్లికి పదేళ్ళు.",
      "gloss": "My little sister is ten.",
      "words": [
        { "te": "చెల్లికి", "gloss": "to little sister" },
        { "te": "పదేళ్ళు", "gloss": "ten years" }
      ],
      "tags": ["age", "family"],
      "difficulty": 2,
      "note": "పది (padi) + ఏళ్ళు (eeLLu) merges into పదేళ్ళు (padeeLLu) 'ten years'. Ages take the dative -కి: చెల్లికి = 'to little sister'.",
      "distractors": ["u02-i12", "u02-i11"]
    },
    {
      "id": "u02-i14",
      "te": "మీ నాన్న ఏం చేస్తారు?",
      "gloss": "What does your father do?",
      "words": [
        { "te": "మీ", "gloss": "your (polite)" },
        { "te": "నాన్న", "gloss": "dad" },
        { "te": "ఏం", "gloss": "what" },
        { "te": "చేస్తారు", "gloss": "does (respectful)" }
      ],
      "tags": ["family", "questions", "work"],
      "difficulty": 2,
      "note": "Respect lives in the verb: dad is one person but gets the plural చేస్తారు (cheestaaru). Singular చేస్తాడు would sound rude here."
    },
    {
      "id": "u02-i15",
      "te": "మా నాన్న డాక్టర్.",
      "gloss": "My dad is a doctor.",
      "words": [
        { "te": "మా", "gloss": "our / my (family)" },
        { "te": "నాన్న", "gloss": "dad" },
        { "te": "డాక్టర్", "gloss": "doctor" }
      ],
      "tags": ["family", "work"],
      "difficulty": 1,
      "distractors": ["u02-i16", "u02-i01"]
    },
    {
      "id": "u02-i16",
      "te": "మా అమ్మ టీచర్.",
      "gloss": "My mom is a teacher.",
      "words": [
        { "te": "మా", "gloss": "our / my (family)" },
        { "te": "అమ్మ", "gloss": "mom" },
        { "te": "టీచర్", "gloss": "teacher" }
      ],
      "tags": ["family", "work"],
      "difficulty": 1,
      "distractors": ["u02-i15", "u02-i02"]
    },
    {
      "id": "u02-i17",
      "te": "మీకు పిల్లలు ఉన్నారా?",
      "gloss": "Do you have children?",
      "words": [
        { "te": "మీకు", "gloss": "to you (polite)" },
        { "te": "పిల్లలు", "gloss": "children" },
        { "te": "ఉన్నారా", "gloss": "are there?" }
      ],
      "tags": ["family", "questions"],
      "difficulty": 2
    }
  ],
